# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.
#
# FIGMA_TOKEN belongs in ~/.fastagents/env, once per machine - one copy per person
# instead of one per project, so rotating it is a single edit. `fa doctor` says which
# source it found.
#
# This file exists for ONE case: a client who insists on their own Figma account. That
# token has to stay inside this repository and must not reach your machine-wide file,
# so it goes here and overrides it.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   git check-ignore -v .env     # confirm it is ignored BEFORE you paste
#
# Read by `fa sitemap-draft` and `fa assets-pull`. Everything else reaches Figma through
# the MCP server, which the kit's ./setup registers and which authenticates separately (/mcp).
#
# The token grants read access to every Figma file the account can open. Treat it like a
# password: never commit it, never paste it into a prompt or a chat.

FIGMA_TOKEN=
